// EXPECT-DIAG: E076
// EXPECT-DIAG: not representable in type 'int32'
// SEM-002 (FREEZE.md §6.2 row 3): the same representability check applies
// to 'int32', not just 'int' -- a literal that fits 'int' comfortably but
// exceeds int32's 32-bit signed range is still rejected, since it's
// acquiring type 'int32' here, not 'int'.
//
// OVH-005 note: before that fix, this test passed for the WRONG reason --
// `mut x: int32 = <literal>;` was unconditionally rejected as an
// 'int -> int32' narrowing (E066, a plain type mismatch) no matter what the
// literal's value was, so this file never actually exercised the E076
// representability check its own comment claims. Confirmed live now: this
// rejects with E076 ("Integer literal is not representable in type
// 'int32'"), citing the exact value 99999999999 and int32's range -- the
// test runner only checks "compilation failed", so this was verified
// manually (`turf --resolve` on this file) rather than by any automated
// per-code assertion; see the OVH-005 change record for the full before/
// after transcript.
fn main(): int {
    mut x: int32 = 99999999999;
    return 0;
}
